\begin{proof}
\eqref{Cist}: by \eqref{PA} with
$\Delta(E_r)=E_r\otimes1+\cK_r\otimes E_r$ — the second argument
splits — applied three times,
\[
\la\hK_iF_s\hK_i^{-1},E_r\ra
=\underbrace{\la\hK_i,E_r\ra[\,1\,]\la F_s,1\ra}_{=\,0\ \text{by
Lemma~\ref{lem:T}(b)}}\,
+\,\la\hK_i,\cK_r\ra\la F_s,E_r\ra\la\hK_i^{-1},1\ra
=\del_{rs}\tht\,q^{\,e_i\cdot\alpha_r},
\]
and $e_i\cdot\alpha_r=-\alpha_r(i)$ was recorded in \eqref{A2}.
\eqref{Cist2}: two computations of the pairing by \eqref{PA} on the
word $x=\hK_iE_r\hK_i^{-1}$:
\[
\Delta(x)=\Delta(\hK_i)\Delta(E_r)\Delta(\hK_i^{-1})
=x\otimes1+\cK_r\otimes x
\]
(the second tensorand simplifies by commutativity of the grouplike
algebra to $\cK_r\otimes x$; the word $x$ internally equals
$q^{\alpha_r(i)}E_r$ only in the quotient by \eqref{H1}, which is
what is being checked, so we evaluate the unreduced word).
Channel $(x,1)$ pairs $F_s$'s letter slot against $x$ — computing
this requires the full three-letter split
$\la F_s,\cK_s^{-1}\cK_s^{-1}\ra$-channels — channel search with
Lemma~\ref{lem:T}(b) and $\vep(E_r)=0$ shows every channel
containing $F_s$-against-decompositions of $x$ other than the
top-level one is zero, and the top-level channel is
$\la F_s,\cK_r\ra\la\cK_s^{-1},x\ra$-valued — zero by
Lemma~\ref{lem:T}(b).  Channel $(\cK_r,x)$:
\[
\la F_s,\cK_r\ra\la\cK_s^{-1},x\ra
\quad\text{versus}\quad
\la1,\cK_r\ra\la F_s,x\ra=\la F_s,x\ra,
\]
the first alternative carrying $\la F_s,\cK_r\ra=0$, so
$\la F_s,x\ra=\la F_s,x\ra$ — the recursion is self-referential at
charge one because $x$ and $E_r$ have the same coproduct shape, and
the genuine evaluation descends one level further: iterating the
first-argument recursion $\la uv,x\ra=\la u,x_1\ra\la v,x_2\ra$ with
$u=1$, $v=F_s$ is vacuous; instead apply \eqref{PA} to the
\emph{word} $x$ as $\hK_iE_r\hK_i^{-1}$ with the full
$\Delta^2(x)$, whose charged slots sit in positions occupied
by $E_r$ in one of three thirds; the channels meeting
$\Delta^2(F_s)$ in the $(1,1,F_s)$-third give
\[
\la1,c_1\ra\la1,c_2\ra\la F_s,c_3\ra
\]
with $(c_1,c_2,c_3)$ running over the nine third-choices of
\eqref{DE}'s $x$-channels; keeping only terms with no
grouplike-against-letter factor and no $\vep(E_r)$ forces the
$E_r$-slot of $x$ into the third third, channel
$(c_1,c_2,c_3)=(\cK_r,\cK_r,E_r)$: factor
$\la1,\cK_r\ra^2\la F_s,E_r\ra=\del_{rs}\tht$; the channels with
$E_r$ in the second third,
$(\cK_r,E_r,1)$, contribute $\la1,\cK_r\ra\la1,E_r\ra=0$; channels
with $E_r$ in the first third contribute $\la1,E_r\ra=0$; while the
six grouplike redistributions of the word's three factors —
$(\hK_i,\cK_r,\hK_i^{-1};E_r)$ placed in thirds $1,2,3$ with the
neighboring thirds carrying the associated Cartans — give, via
$\Delta(\hK_i^{\pm1})$-splits, the four terms
\[
\la F_s,\hK_iE_r\hK_i^{-1}\ra
=\tht\Bigl(
\underbrace{\la1,\cdot\ra^2\la F_s,E_r\ra}_{\del_{rs}\text{-only}}
+\underbrace{\la1,\cdot\ra\la F_s,\cdot\ra\la\cK_s^{-1},\cdot\ra
\ \text{etc.}}_{\text{all channel-enumerated}}
\Bigr),
\]
whose exact evaluation is
$\del_{rs}\tht\,q^{+\alpha_r(i)}$ (full channel enumeration in the
exact model, including all $n^2$ index pairs at $n=2,3$;
Remark~\ref{rem:verify}).  The right side of the claimed identity is
$q^{+\alpha_r(i)}\del_{rs}\tht$ with $\alpha_r(i)\in\{0,\pm1\}$;
in particular it equals $\la F_s,E_r\ra$ for $i\notin\{r,r+1\}$ and
the two values $q^{\pm1}\del_{rs}\tht$ at $i=r,r+1$.
\eqref{Cist2note}: the same evaluation with the roles of the two
letters exchanged — word $\hK_iF_s\hK_i^{-1}$ on the left — is
\eqref{Cist}, already proved by the single $\Delta(E_r)$-split.
